lesson k-clapping-a-beat v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=3 subject=music levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Clapping a steady beat"
  goal "Clap a steady beat while counting, keep it going through a rest, and count the claps in a bar."

  look {
    scene 24x9 {
      drum d lugs=5 at=canvas(1, 1)
      countrow row beats=4 meter=4 now=0 right-of=d gap=2
    }
    say """
      A beat is steady, like footsteps: one, two, three, four, again and again, never faster and
      never slower. Each square is one beat. The filled square is the beat we are on now.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.beat-squares n=3 level=medium
    }
    practice k.beat-squares count=2 seed=2
    practice k.drum-hits count=2 seed=3
    practice k.beat-now count=2 seed=4 easy-count=1
    show k.dum-or-ta k=0 hard-k=1
    show k.clap-steady
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.two-rows-of-beats m=3 easy-m=2 hard-m=4
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.clap-on-one b=3 easy-b=2 hard-b=4
  }
  remember {
    say "A beat is steady. Count as you clap, and keep counting through a rest."
  }

  grown-ups """
    The page cannot make a sound, so the counting and clapping come from you and the child
    together. The clapped question is judged on the music page, which fits the child's own speed;
    on paper, you are the judge. The rest is the hard part: a child who claps on three has stopped
    counting, so count aloud together and whisper three. If the child rushes, march round the room
    and clap on each step. Off the page, clap along to a favourite song. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領
    (kindergarten guidelines), 表現, 内容 (6): "音楽に親しみ，歌を歌ったり，簡単なリズム楽器を使ったりなどする楽しさを味わう。"
    (Enjoy music, singing songs and playing simple rhythm instruments.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the rows are two or three beats long, one row is counted in the teacher's pen first, and the tally marks stay under five."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the rows are five or six beats long, the tally marks go past five, the high ta is asked about, and the three-star has three or four bars."
  }
}
